.TH CHTTP_REQUEST_NEW_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_request_new_mp \- allocate and initialise an HTTP request with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttp_request_t *chttp_request_new_mp(chttp_method_t method,
                                      const char *url,
                                      const chttp_request_body_t *body,
                                      ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mprocs,
                                      char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a new chttp_request_t and copies the URL and, if non-NULL,
the body data and content_type string into privately owned buffers.
The caller may free its originals immediately after this call returns.

Pass NULL for body or use the CHTTP_NO_BODY macro when no request body
is needed (e.g. GET, DELETE). body->data may be NULL only when
body->len == 0; a NULL body->data paired with a nonzero body->len is
rejected (returns NULL) rather than silently treated as no body.

The returned request's expect_continue field defaults to false (the
struct is zero-initialised). Set it to true after construction (e.g.
req->expect_continue = true) to send "Expect: 100-continue" and wait
for the server's interim response before sending the body; see
chttpclient_do(3) for the full protocol. Has no effect on a request
with no body, or one that already has an explicit "Expect" header set
via chttp_request_set_header. Honored uniformly by every tier
(chttpclient_do/chttpclient_do_streaming, chttpclient_do_async/
chttpclient_do_async_streaming, and chttpclient_do_pooled/
chttpclient_do_pooled_streaming).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
method    HTTP method (CHTTP_GET, CHTTP_POST, ...).
url       Target URL; must not be NULL (copied into the request).
body      Pointer to a chttp_request_body_t, or NULL for no body.
mprocs    Custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
err_str   Optional; receives a static error string on failure.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Pointer to the new request, or NULL on failure (including a NULL url,
a NULL body->data with a nonzero body->len, or allocation failure).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
All allocations use mprocs when non-NULL.
The request must remain alive until any chttpclient_do call using it
returns: the request's method/body/headers are read directly during
that synchronous call.

body->content_type is copied verbatim here with no validation (this
function cannot yet know whether it will even be used on the wire; an
explicit "content-type" header set later via chttp_request_set_header
takes precedence and suppresses it). If it reaches serialization time
still containing an embedded CR or LF byte, the chttpclient_do/
chttp_run_query/etc. call using this request fails with
ccol_invalid_args instead of writing it onto the wire; see
chttp_request_set_header(3) for why.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_new (3),
.BR chttp_request_set_header (3),
.BR chttp_request_free (3),
.BR chttpclient_do (3)
